# Global Cursor Agent Rules (AFS)

Follow `~/src/docs/guides/ai-coder/AGENT_HARNESS_CONTRACT.md`,
`~/src/docs/guides/ai-coder/AGENT_COMMUNICATION_STANDARD.md`, and
`~/src/docs/guides/ai-coder/AGENT_STORAGE_HYGIENE.md`. Project `AGENTS.md`
files add local constraints and take precedence.

## AFS Context & Slim Tool Surface
- Rely on the `SessionStart` bootstrap packet or run `<AFS_ROOT>/scripts/afs session bootstrap --short --path <workspace> --json` once at startup.
- Use the frozen 16-tool slim AFS MCP catalog (`context.status`, `context.query`, `context.read`, `context.list`, `context.write`, `messages.*`, `note.*`, `handoff.*`, `skill.*`); avoid deprecated `fs.*` aliases.
- Store shared handoffs and evidence in `scratchpad/`, durable discoveries only in `note.*` / `handoff.*`, and update `memory/` or `knowledge/` only on user request.
- Use `afs search --semantic --provider auto "<query>"` (run `afs embeddings probe` to verify local LM Studio / Ollama / MLX backends before falling back to cloud).

## Communication & Judgment Calls
1. Put the result or next action first; preserve exact commands, paths, identifiers, and errors.
2. Decide mechanical and low-stakes reversible calls yourself in one line.
3. For judgment calls (architecture, design, priority, taste), lead with your pick, give 2–4 numbered options with costs, ask one question, and state disagreements before acting.
4. Report changed files, verification commands run with observed outcomes, and remaining limitations.
